#46251
"Small Farm Road"
"The road is just wide enough for a one-horse cart to pass, and a well-worn rut

in the center indicates it is used for just that purpose.  It is a simple dirt

road, clear from grass and growth, but turns to pure mud in the rain.  The

road leads west towards a large house in the distance and east into an old

forest, quickly becoming a narrower path.  On either side of the fences you can

see a wheat field to the north and an orchard south.

"
""
