ready to prepare the next meal.  A large fireplace is in the wall to the west,

kept lit for cooking at all times, which makes the kitchen uncomfortably

warm.  Next to the fireplace is a stove for baking and cooking smaller things

when the fireplace is in use.  A window in the southern wall, opened just a

crack, provides the only relief to the heat.  The door to the pantry is east

and the dining room is through the north doorway.

