"A long wooden table takes up most of the space in this dining room, leaving

just barely enough room for the chairs lining it to be pulled out.  A

landscape painting decorates the north wall, bringing a bit of color to the

whitewashed walls of the kitchen.  Hot air wafts out of the kitchen to the

south and past the entryway to the east is the door of the farmhouse.  The

foggy glass window of the west wall lets in light but has no way of being

opened, showing just vague splotches of color of the outside fields.

